    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0020" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg12"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">756.94/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-22T13:00:00+09:00">April 22, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 22—1:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>273. Our 269, April 20, 5 p.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d12-f1"/> This morning’s
                    vernacular press reports that, after an interview with the Secretary of State on
                    April 20, Ambassador Horinouchi announced that Japan and the United States have
                    reached an agreement in principle with regard to the question of the maintenance
                    of the <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi> of the Dutch East Indies.<anchor
                        n="31" xml:id="d12-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
